/* Constant tables for math: a 128-entry logarithm table and a 128-entry table of powers of 2 for
 * exp, log, and pow, and the bits of 2/pi for the sin and cos reduction of large arguments.
 *
 * The first two are derived here from first principles with 100-digit arithmetic.
 *
 * log: x = 2^k * z with z in [OFF, 2*OFF), OFF the bit pattern 0x3FE7100000000000, which puts
 * 1.0 inside one interval so that interval can use c = 1 exactly. Bits 45..51 of (bits(x) - OFF)
 * select entry i; its z-interval spans bit patterns OFF + i*2^45 up to OFF + (i+1)*2^45. With m the
 * interval's centre, invc is round(128/m)/128 for m < 1 and round(256/m)/256 otherwise, so
 * |z*invc - 1| stays under 2^-7 and invc is a short binary fraction: z*invc - 1 is then exact
 * once z is split into two halves. c = 1/invc; logc is ln(c) rounded to a multiple of 2^-41, so
 * k*ln2hi + logc is exact, and logctail is the double nearest ln(c) - logc.
 *
 * two_bits[j] is the bit pattern of the double nearest 2^(j/128), and two_tail[j] is the relative
 * correction (2^(j/128) - s) / s, so 2^(j/128) = s * (1 + tail).
 */

pub Log: struct {
    invc: f64,
    logc: f64,
    logctail: f64,
}

